1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:07,077
Welcome to lesson 4.2 of the Brightwell CCM technical training.

2
00:00:07,277 --> 00:00:12,963
It has six parts. In part one, you enroll a scratch patient in Chronic Care Management,

3
00:00:13,003 --> 00:00:17,057
record their consent, and open the initial assessment.

4
00:00:18,957 --> 00:00:21,932
Here's what you've done so far for this patient.

5
00:00:22,232 --> 00:00:26,977
You received the patient task, and its type is scratch: a new patient.

6
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:31,370
You found the patient in PointClickCare, and checked eligibility:

7
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:34,326
the patient is active in the facility.

8
00:00:34,626 --> 00:00:37,602
You used the ICD-10 code to find the condition,

9
00:00:37,642 --> 00:00:43,019
and made sure it's eligible, and that the patient takes a medication for it.

10
00:00:43,319 --> 00:00:47,382
You wrote the problem note, the template for the patient's care plan.

11
00:00:47,682 --> 00:00:53,905
And because this is a scratch patient, you created the patient's profile in ThoroughCare, from scratch.

12
00:00:54,205 --> 00:00:57,052
A scratch patient needs one more job.

13
00:00:57,352 --> 00:01:03,911
You enroll the patient in CCM, record their consent, and add their CCM condition.

14
00:01:04,211 --> 00:01:08,743
Then you complete the initial assessment, which parts two to six cover.

15
00:01:12,043 --> 00:01:17,620
When you open the patient's profile in ThoroughCare, you see many tabs across the page.

16
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:22,743
You do all of your work in two of them: Clinical Data, and Care Management.

17
00:01:22,993 --> 00:01:28,784
Clinical Data holds the patient's clinical lists, such as conditions and allergies.

18
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:33,003
Enrollment starts in the other one. Click Care Management.

19
00:01:34,376 --> 00:01:39,505
Care Management opens on the CCM tab, for Chronic Care Management.

20
00:01:39,755 --> 00:01:43,306
This is where you work with the patient's CCM program.

21
00:01:44,613 --> 00:01:48,356
Scroll down the CCM tab to Program Setup.

22
00:01:54,110 --> 00:01:58,621
Here is Enrollment And Consent. Its status is Not Enrolled.

23
00:01:58,871 --> 00:02:05,131
Assign Care Team already has a check mark, with the care manager and provider from the profile.

24
00:02:05,381 --> 00:02:11,406
Enrollment and consent is a first-time step. You do it only once, for a scratch patient.

25
00:02:11,656 --> 00:02:16,807
Once the patient is enrolled, they're a follow-up patient, and you don't repeat it.

26
00:02:17,057 --> 00:02:19,285
Click Enrollment And Consent.

27
00:02:20,643 --> 00:02:26,668
The CCM Enrollment Status window opens. The current status is Not Enrolled.

28
00:02:26,928 --> 00:02:30,201
Click the box under Change enrollment status to.

29
00:02:30,451 --> 00:02:37,976
The list has one active status, Active, and inactive ones, such as Considering, Decline, and Ineligible.

30
00:02:38,226 --> 00:02:41,521
This patient is active, so select Active.

31
00:02:42,876 --> 00:02:48,368
Below are five statements, under Patients must consent and agree to the following.

32
00:02:48,624 --> 00:02:52,606
The patient must agree to all five, so check every box.

33
00:02:52,861 --> 00:03:00,716
Patient agrees to participate in CCM & PCM. Patient understands that there may be a copay,

34
00:03:00,756 --> 00:03:04,326
and that they can cancel CCM & PCM.

35
00:03:04,910 --> 00:03:12,749
Information can be shared with other providers, and only one practitioner can bill for CCM & PCM.

36
00:03:13,013 --> 00:03:15,570
For Consent method, choose Verbal.

37
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:22,351
Updated by and Start Date are filled in for you, and Patient is Billable stays checked.

38
00:03:22,601 --> 00:03:24,253
Then click Save.

39
00:03:25,576 --> 00:03:30,492
Enrollment And Consent now has a check mark, and its status is Active.

40
00:03:30,743 --> 00:03:37,963
Next, the Edit Patient Conditions window opens. Here you add the condition the patient is enrolled for.

41
00:03:38,213 --> 00:03:45,156
Use the condition you confirmed in PointClickCare. For this patient, it's I10: hypertension.

42
00:03:45,415 --> 00:03:47,243
Click Add condition.

43
00:03:47,493 --> 00:03:52,537
A list of conditions opens. Type the first letters, hyper, to filter it.

44
00:03:52,792 --> 00:03:54,977
Then select Hypertension.

45
00:03:57,343 --> 00:04:00,851
Hypertension is now on the list of conditions.

46
00:04:01,101 --> 00:04:05,872
Because it's the only chronic condition, a note says the patient's care

47
00:04:05,912 --> 00:04:10,817
will be managed under Principal Care Management (PCM) guidelines.

48
00:04:11,067 --> 00:04:15,215
Under Programs, make sure the condition is set to CCM.

49
00:04:16,543 --> 00:04:21,950
Next, under Diagnosis Code, add the ICD-10 code for the condition.

50
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:27,607
Use the exact code from PointClickCare. Some conditions have several codes.

51
00:04:27,857 --> 00:04:34,544
Type 2 diabetes, for example, can be E11.22 or E11.40.

52
00:04:34,794 --> 00:04:37,491
Click Add From Diagnosis History.

53
00:04:39,610 --> 00:04:46,169
The list shows codes commonly used for hypertension. If the patient's code is there, select it.

54
00:04:46,419 --> 00:04:48,839
Scroll the list to see more codes.

55
00:04:49,788 --> 00:04:52,635
If the code isn't listed, click Add New.

56
00:04:52,885 --> 00:04:55,924
Search for the code. Here, type I10.

57
00:04:57,525 --> 00:04:59,902
Select the code, and click Save.

58
00:05:01,076 --> 00:05:07,336
The code now appears next to the condition: I10 - Essential (primary) hypertension.

59
00:05:08,643 --> 00:05:10,490
Click Save and Close.

60
00:05:11,610 --> 00:05:17,123
The window closes, and the CCM tab now shows the Initial Monthly Workflow.

61
00:05:17,373 --> 00:05:24,849
So far, the patient is enrolled, consent is recorded, and the CCM condition and its code are added.

62
00:05:25,109 --> 00:05:27,721
Scroll up to check the top of the tab.

63
00:05:28,210 --> 00:05:31,419
CCM now has a check mark next to it.

64
00:05:31,683 --> 00:05:36,578
Under CCM Conditions, you see Hypertension, with code I10.

65
00:05:36,828 --> 00:05:43,125
And under Program Status, Chronic Care Management and Principal Care Management are now Active.

66
00:05:44,443 --> 00:05:47,930
Scroll back down to the Initial Monthly Workflow.

67
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:54,634
For a scratch patient, there's one more first-time task: the Initial Patient-Centered Care Plan.

68
00:05:54,884 --> 00:05:59,203
It's a short assessment that you do once, when the patient is enrolled.

69
00:05:59,457 --> 00:06:02,368
Click Initial Patient-Centered Care Plan.

70
00:06:03,710 --> 00:06:09,735
A window opens, to choose the chronic conditions managed under the CCM program.

71
00:06:09,985 --> 00:06:14,133
It notes that ICD-10 codes aren't required to begin a care plan,

72
00:06:14,173 --> 00:06:18,272
but they must be added before any claims are submitted.

73
00:06:18,522 --> 00:06:23,822
Check that the condition is right, the code is right, and the program is CCM.

74
00:06:24,072 --> 00:06:26,705
Then click Save and Start Assessment.

75
00:06:28,843 --> 00:06:33,241
The initial assessment opens, with its sections listed on the left.

76
00:06:33,491 --> 00:06:41,564
You'll complete the General Health Questionnaire, Support, Allergies, Medications, and Numbers to Track, one part at a time.

77
00:06:42,976 --> 00:06:44,500
Let's recap.

78
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:51,749
Open Care Management, and on the CCM tab, click Enrollment And Consent, under Program Setup.

79
00:06:51,949 --> 00:06:57,761
Set the status to Active, check all five consent statements, choose Verbal, and save.

80
00:06:57,961 --> 00:07:06,717
Add the CCM condition, keep its program as CCM, and add the exact ICD-10 code from PointClickCare.

81
00:07:06,917 --> 00:07:14,585
Save and close. Then open the Initial Patient-Centered Care Plan, check it, and click Save and Start Assessment.

82
00:07:16,785 --> 00:07:23,322
That's part one. The patient is enrolled in CCM, and the initial assessment is open.

83
00:07:23,522 --> 00:07:27,265
In part two, you answer the General Health Questionnaire.
